A last-resort route for volume keys the firmware fully swallows

Some devices don't even hand the volume press to the audio system — they just change the volume themselves. The new second stage (Settings, below the audio route switch) detects that change, silently undoes it, and treats it as the key press it was. Single, double and long press all work.

Deliberately off by default: only needed where the keys don't show up otherwise. Won't touch active media playback.
